erification.json"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a274246d52f520fddc7ecf4f3e9e3ba6705721a24b41e8b687ff9461311e76d" "basis" 2509 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-3+5\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(4-3\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i}) \\\\ (-4\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(5-5\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(15+9\\text{i})+(1-32\\text{i}) \\\\ (-12)+(-5-45\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a274246d52f520fddc7ecf4f3e9e3ba6705721a24b41e8b687ff9461311e76d" "basis" 2509 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/activ